WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.920
The question you are actually asking.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.544
“Which model is best?

3
00:00:03.824 --> 00:00:05.019
” has no answer.

4
00:00:05.299 --> 00:00:10.205
“Which model is good enough for this task, at the lowest cost and risk, and how do I know?

5
00:00:10.485 --> 00:00:11.253
” does.

6
00:00:11.533 --> 00:00:26.893
This lesson gives you three things: what each provider says its models are for (claims), what independent measurement shows (evidence, with caveats), and a playbook that ends in the only evidence that settles your question, a small eval on your own task.

7
00:00:27.173 --> 00:00:31.504
Studio 1, lesson 3 introduced the landscape and the pricing math.

8
00:00:31.784 --> 00:00:41.832
This lesson is the decision layer on top: how to weigh distinctive features against raw capability, and how to build checks into the choice so you notice when it goes stale.

9
00:00:42.112 --> 00:00:44.203
A warning about this lesson’s shelf life.

10
00:00:44.483 --> 00:00:51.288
Everything below was checked on 11 November 2026, and model lineups change every few months.

11
00:00:51.568 --> 00:00:56.176
The structure of the decision (features, evidence, eval) will outlast the names.

12
00:00:56.456 --> 00:01:04.477
When you use this lesson later, reread the providers’ pages first; if a model named here no longer exists, the method still applies.
